{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaouEaqT2T5fhbFp755K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've proved `fib_le_pow` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\nThe proof uses a stronger statement: for every `m`, both `fib m ≤ 2^m` and `fib (m+1) ≤ 2^(m+1)` hold. I proved that by induction on `m`:\n- **Base case:** `fib 0 = 0 ≤ 1` and `fib 1 = 1 ≤ 2`, which `decide` checks directly.\n- **Inductive step:** The first half of the new pair is the second half of the old one. For the second half, `fib (k+2) = fib k + fib (k+1) ≤ 2^k + 2^(k+1) ≤ 2^(k+2)`. After rewriting the powers with `Nat.pow_succ`, `omega` handles that inequality.\n\nThe theorem is then the first half of this statement at `m = n`.\n\nThe stronger statement is needed because each Fibonacci number depends on the two before it. Plain induction would only give the bound for the previous number."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1090,"cache_read_input_tokens":7919,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1090},"output_tokens":350,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7c3cab1-8677-4acb-8f02-e260d0e4d4d0","uuid":"6c79d150-7c07-474c-a58c-a2f7511dd4f0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T18:44:35.717Z","request_id":"req_011CgaouENSJQp5o3dXHSz56"}
